Keep a shared source as empty text.
Place "abcd" into source.
Keep a shared indices as an empty list of whole numbers.
Place 2 into indices.
Place 0 into indices.
Keep a shared sources as an empty list of text.
Place "cd" into sources.
Place "a" into sources.
Keep a shared targets as an empty list of text.
Place "ffff" into targets.
Place "eee" into targets.
Keep a shared used as an empty list of whole numbers.
Place 0 into used.
Place 0 into used.
Keep a shared ordercount as 0.
Set ordercount to 2.
Keep a shared best as 0.
Keep a shared pick as 0.
Keep a shared cursor as 0.
Keep a shared result as empty text.

To seek from slot (a whole number).
If slot is at least ordercount, return.
If item slot of used is 0 and item slot of indices is less than best.
Set best to item slot of indices.
Set pick to slot.
Seek from slot plus 1.

To render from spot (a whole number) with slot (a whole number).
If spot is less than cursor, return.
The head is the slice of source from cursor to spot.
Place head into result.
Set cursor to spot.
The pattern is item slot of sources.
The patternlast is the last position of pattern.
The size is patternlast plus 1.
The finish is spot plus size.
The piece is the slice of source from spot to finish.
If piece matches pattern, Place item slot of targets into result.
If piece matches pattern, Set cursor to finish.
If piece does not match pattern, Place piece into result.
If piece does not match pattern, Set cursor to finish.

The step is 0.
Repeat while step is less than ordercount.
Set best to 1000000.
Set pick to -1.
Seek from 0.
The slot is pick.
Set item slot of used to 1.
The spot is item slot of indices.
Render from spot with slot.
Set step to step plus 1.

The endspot is the last position of source.
The tail is the slice of source from cursor to endspot plus 1.
Place tail into result.
Show result.
